//RS /// The arena half of `jet_jit_list_unzip`, split from the runtime borrow so it
//RS /// can be pinned without a resident runtime.
//RS ///
//RS /// #2091: the gate arm and the lowering now read ONE table
//RS /// (`LowerCtx::unzip_column_kinds`), so the last pairing under `.unzip()` that
//RS /// can still drift is the per-kind representation pair inside this file — the
//RS /// writer `jit_zip_set_value` against the readers `jit_zip_record_field` and
//RS /// `jit_zip_read_value`. That pair is exactly what shipped two EMPTY lists, and
//RS /// it is a pure set over `JitZipValueKind`, so `unzip_column_round_trip` below
//RS /// checks it instead of leaving a stem as the only witness.
