//RS /// The one pairing `.unzip()` still has on both sides of a representation
//RS /// boundary: `jit_zip_set_value` writes a column word, `jit_zip_record_field`
//RS /// reads it back out of the row, and `jit_zip_read_value` reads it back out of
//RS /// the republished column. Total over `JitZipValueKind`, so it is checkable as
//RS /// a set — unlike the `TBuiltinOp` lowering halves, which need a live
//RS /// `FunctionBuilder` (#2091).
//RS #[cfg(test)]
